{
  "id": "resistor_standard_values",
  "title": "Resistor Standard Values",
  "description": "Preferred number series for resistors according IEC 60063. Calculate voltage, resistance, and current using Ohm's Law.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Resistor Standard Values\n\nPreferred number series for resistors according IEC 60063 are indicated below.\n\n### Resistors with 10% tolerance\n\nStandard values: 10, 12, 15, 18, 22, 27, 33, 39, 47, 56, 68, 82 (ohm, kohm, and higher decades)\n\n### Resistors with 5% tolerance\n\nStandard values: 10, 11, 12, 13, 15, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24, 27, 30, 33, 36, 39, 43, 47, 51, 56, 62, 68, 75, 82, 91 (ohm, kohm, and higher decades)\n\n### Ohm's Law\n\nOhm's law can be expressed as:\n\n**U = R × I** (Voltage = Resistance × Current)\n\nor\n\n**R = U / I** (Resistance = Voltage / Current)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "voltage",
          "label": "Voltage (U)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "V",
          "defaultValue": 5
        },
        {
          "id": "current",
          "label": "Current (I)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "A",
          "defaultValue": 0.1
        },
        {
          "id": "resistance",
          "label": "Resistance (R)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Ω",
          "defaultValue": 50
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "calculated_resistance",
          "label": "Calculated Resistance",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage / inputs.current",
          "unit": "Ω",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "calculated_voltage",
          "label": "Calculated Voltage",
          "formula": "inputs.resistance * inputs.current",
          "unit": "V",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "calculated_current",
          "label": "Calculated Current",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage / inputs.resistance",
          "unit": "A",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "power",
          "label": "Power (P)",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage * inputs.current",
          "unit": "W",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Tolerance",
        "10% Standard Values",
        "5% Standard Values"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Base Series",
          "10, 12, 15, 18, 22, 27, 33, 39, 47, 56, 68, 82",
          "10, 11, 12, 13, 15, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24, 27, 30, 33, 36, 39, 43, 47, 51, 56, 62, 68, 75, 82, 91"
        ],
        [
          "Example (Ω)",
          "10Ω, 12Ω, 15Ω, 18Ω, 22Ω, 27Ω, 33Ω, 39Ω, 47Ω, 56Ω, 68Ω, 82Ω",
          "10Ω, 11Ω, 12Ω, 13Ω, 15Ω, 16Ω, 18Ω, 20Ω, 22Ω, 24Ω, 27Ω, 30Ω, 33Ω, 36Ω, 39Ω, 43Ω, 47Ω, 51Ω, 56Ω, 62Ω, 68Ω, 75Ω, 82Ω, 91Ω"
        ],
        [
